section: ghc-lib
synopsis:
  The External Package State is an abstract, query-only handle; GHC API users
  can install their own implementation with ``GHC.setExternalPackageStore``
description:
  ``GHC.Unit.External.ExternalPackageState`` is now an abstract record of
  operations rather than a record of maps. The rest of GHC only queries it
  (``eps_lookupTyThing``, ``eps_lookupIface``, ``eps_getInstEnv``, ...) and adds
  freshly loaded modules to it (``eps_addModule`` with an ``EpsModule``). GHC's
  own implementation still keeps everything in memory
  (``GHC.Unit.External.InMemory``).

  GHC API users can implement their own store (for example one that keeps the
  declarations of loaded modules on disk and typechecks them again on demand
  with ``epm_rehydrate``, trading speed for memory) with the constructor
  exported by ``GHC.Unit.External.Store``. They install it with
  ``GHC.setExternalPackageStore`` (or ``GHC.Driver.Env.hscSetEPS``) before
  anything is loaded. ``GHC.Unit.External.Iface.setExternalIfaceHashFn`` and
  ``GHC.Iface.Load.readIfaceCopying`` are exported for such stores.

  Breaking changes:

  * The fields ``eps_PTE``, ``eps_ext_ifaces``, ``eps_inst_env``,
    ``eps_fam_inst_env``, ``eps_rule_base``, ... are gone; use the query
    functions of ``GHC.Unit.External``.
  * ``GHC.Driver.Env.hscEPS`` and ``GHC.Unit.Env.ueEPS`` are pure, and
    ``lookupExternalIface`` is in ``IO``.
  * ``GHC.Tc.Utils.Monad.updateEps``, ``updateEps_`` and ``getEpsVar`` are
    removed, as is ``GHC.Driver.Env.lookupTypeInPTE``.
  * ``GHC.Iface.Load.ifaceStats`` takes an ``EpsStats``.
